PKGUTIL(3)

# NAME

pkgutil - package database and installation utility

# SYNOPSIS

```
#include <libpkgcore/pkgutil.h>

class pkgutil {
public:
    pkgutil(const std::string& name);

    void db_open(const std::string& path);
    void db_commit();

    void db_add_pkg(const std::string& name, const pkginfo_t& info);
    bool db_find_pkg(const std::string& name);

    void db_rm_pkg(const std::string& name);
    void db_rm_pkg(const std::string& name,
                   const std::set<std::string>& keep_list);

    void db_rm_files(std::set<std::string> files,
                     const std::set<std::string>& keep_list);

    std::set<std::string>
    db_find_conflicts(const std::string& name,
                      const pkginfo_t& info);

    std::pair<std::string, pkginfo_t>
    pkg_open(const std::string& filename) const;

    void pkg_install(const std::string& filename,
                     const std::set<std::string>& keep_list,
                     const std::set<std::string>& non_install_list,
                     bool upgrade) const;

    void ldconfig() const;
    void pkg_footprint(const std::string& filename) const;
    void print_version() const;

    const packages_t& getPackages() const;
};
```

# DESCRIPTION

*pkgutil* encapsulates package database state and package
manipulation operations.

It maintains an in-memory map of installed packages and provides
methods for synchronization with on-disk state.

# STATE

Internal state includes:

- root (filesystem root)
- packages (map of installed packages)

*db\_open()* must be called before most operations.

# DATABASE OPERATIONS

*db\_open()*
	Loads package database into memory.

*db\_commit()*
	Writes in-memory state to disk using a safe write strategy.

*db\_add\_pkg()*
	Adds package to in-memory database.

*db\_find\_pkg()*
	Checks for existence.

*db\_rm\_pkg()*
	Removes package and deletes owned files.

*db\_rm\_files()*
	Removes files and updates ownership records.

*db\_find\_conflicts()*
	Detects file conflicts with existing packages.

# PACKAGE OPERATIONS

*pkg\_open()*
	Reads package archive and extracts metadata.

*pkg\_install()*
	Extracts archive to filesystem and updates state.

	Behavior modifiers:
		- keep_list: do not overwrite/remove these paths
		- non_install_list: skip extraction
		- upgrade: alters conflict semantics

*pkg\_footprint()*
	Prints archive contents in footprint format.

# SYSTEM INTEGRATION

*ldconfig()*
	Executes system ldconfig utility.

*print\_version()*
	Outputs library version and feature information.

# ERROR HANDLING

All mutating and I/O operations throw *std::runtime\_error* on failure.

Partial state mutation may occur before failure.

No transactional rollback is guaranteed.

# SIGNALS AND INTERRUPTION

Constructing a *pkgutil* object does not install signal handlers or
alter the calling thread's signal mask.

The caller owns process signal policy.
Read-only consumers normally need no special handling.
Consumers composing mutating primitives must define the critical
section in which interruption is accepted, deferred, or translated
into cooperative cancellation.

Deferring *SIGHUP*, *SIGINT*, *SIGQUIT*, or *SIGTERM* around a
mutation sequence may prevent user-requested termination between
related filesystem and database operations.
It does not provide rollback and does not protect against *SIGKILL*,
crashes, I/O failures, or power loss.

# INVARIANTS

- packages map reflects last successful *db\_open*/*db\_commit* cycle
- file ownership must remain consistent across packages
- *db\_commit()* is required for persistence

# THREAD SAFETY

Not thread-safe.

# NOTES

The class combines:

- database logic
- filesystem mutation
- archive handling

Callers must enforce correct sequencing and locking.

# SEE ALSO

*db\_lock*(3),
*fs\_utils*(3),
*libpkgcore*(7)

